{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the safety chain: it repeatedly triaged current neurologic/raised-ICP symptoms, treated obstructive hydrocephalus as time-sensitive, avoided over-reading unclear records, directed prompt neurosurgical/inpatient pathways, and closed discharge with medication, wound, red-flag, pathology, and follow-up plans. It also completed multiple high-order opportunities, including correcting benign/pathology misconceptions, verifying ambiguous surgical/pathology interpretations, repairing ownership of pathology/discharge tasks, and dynamically escalating from outpatient document sorting to ED/inpatient pathways when access barriers appeared. There is no serious or minor responsibility-chain error evident, and closure is safe and executable despite a nonurgent final clarification request that had largely been answered earlier. Grade 5 is warranted because the performance satisfies Strong and completes at least two case-defined high-order points with meaningful trajectory impact.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00813",
        "explanation": "Doctor translated discharge red flags into an actionable home safety rule.",
        "quote": "烧、漏、痛、吐、困、抽、偏"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00839",
        "explanation": "Doctor made home medication execution safe by requiring clarification before dosing and forbidding self-stopping key medicines.",
        "quote": "左乙拉西坦和激素类药都不能自己停"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00859",
        "explanation": "Doctor converted the steroid taper into an executable day-by-day schedule.",
        "quote": "第1天和第2天：早2、中2、晚2"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00873",
        "explanation": "Family demonstrated receipt and execution of the discharge medication plan.",
        "quote": "晚上的药喂完了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode reached a safe discharge/home-care state: medications were reconciled, steroid taper was made executable, red flags and emergency thresholds were clear, wound care and follow-up were explained, and the family demonstrated initial implementation. The last family message asked for further simplification about pathology follow-up, but that issue had already been addressed as nonurgent follow-up rather than a blocking safety gap.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00093",
